{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Decision Boundary.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Decision Boundary.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"decision boundary decision boundary","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Decision Boundary.md","fileName":"Decision Boundary.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Decision Boundary","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 00:13\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Neural Network Training]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Neural Network Training","Classifier","Perceptron","Artificial Neural Network","Neural Network Bias","Model Input Space","algorithms.epub","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Decision Boundary.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Decision Boundary.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"decision boundary decision boundary","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Decision Boundary.md","fileName":"Decision Boundary.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Decision Boundary","heading":"Decision Boundary","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A decision boundary separates the regions of input space that a [[Classifier]] assigns to different outcomes. In two dimensions it can be visualized as a line or curve between classes.\n\nA single [[Perceptron]] can learn only a linear boundary, so it handles data that can be divided by one straight line. An [[Artificial Neural Network]] with hidden layers can combine neuron outputs to represent more complicated, nonlinear boundaries.\n\nKelleher's two-input threshold-neuron example makes the geometry concrete. The boundary is perpendicular to the neuron's input-weight vector; altering the weights rotates it, while a [[Neural Network Bias|bias term]] moves it off the origin. That separates the effects of weight direction and threshold position on which [[Model Input Space|input points]] receive high activation.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Neural Network Training","Classifier","Perceptron","Artificial Neural Network","Neural Network Bias","Model Input Space","algorithms.epub","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Decision Boundary.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Decision Boundary.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"decision boundary decision boundary","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Decision Boundary.md","fileName":"Decision Boundary.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Decision Boundary","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[algorithms.epub]]\n\n[[deeplearning_mit.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Neural Network Training","Classifier","Perceptron","Artificial Neural Network","Neural Network Bias","Model Input Space","algorithms.epub","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}